error[E0609]: the tag `Bad` appears in both layers of this nested error row with different payloads
 --> mem:///main.lu:1:40
  |
1 | fn poke(n: int) -> int ! {Bad(int)} ! {Bad(str)} {
  |                                        ^^^^^^^^ `Bad(str)` here, `Bad(int)` in the inner layer
  |
  = note: a nested error row flattens to one union ([gram.type.row.flatten]): tag names are
    structural, so the same name in two layers is the same tag, and one tag carries one
    payload shape. Layers that must stay separable are a nominal wrapper type — wrap one
    payload and the tags stop colliding.
help: wrap this layer's payload in a nominal type of its own (`type BadWrapped = distinct str`)
  |
1 | fn poke(n: int) -> int ! {Bad(int)} ! {Bad(BadWrapped)} {
  |
